    "problem_statement": "Forbidden class initialization broken after recent changes\n\n#### Description\n\nThe `Forbidden` class is not working properly - it's throwing `AttributeError` when trying to create instances. This affects validation of forbidden keys in schemas.\n\n#### Steps/Code to Reproduce\n\n```python\nfrom schema import Schema, Forbidden\n\n# This should work but throws an error\ntry:\n    s = Schema({Forbidden('forbidden'): str, 'test': str})\n    print(\"Schema created successfully\")\nexcept Exception as e:\n    print(f\"Error creating schema: {e}\")\n\n# This should also work\ntry:\n    forbidden_schema = Schema({Forbidden('b'): object})\n    result = forbidden_schema.validate({'b': 'bye'})\nexcept Exception as e:\n    print(f\"Error during validation: {e}\")\n```\n\n#### Expected Behavior\n\nThe `Forbidden` class should initialize properly and allow validation of schemas with forbidden keys.\n\n#### Actual Behavior\n\nGetting `AttributeError: 'Forbidden' object has no attribute '_alternate_function'` when trying to create `Forbidden` instances."
  }
